00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.440
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: proceed, Senator Judge Cayetano is recognized.

00:22:40.660 --> 00:23:49.900
Sen. Alan Peter Cayetano: That we also need time to study. So if we look at our rules of impeachment, suppletory kasi yung rules ng rules of court. And the difference between asking the accused to take the stand and asking someone who is not the accused, but we may say something that is incriminatory. There's a wide difference. So the accused, under the rules of court, hindi mo pwedeng i-force to take the stand. Pero yung hindi accused, they have to take the stand and wait for the question and then they can claim the right against self-incrimination. But it could be argued that this isn't exactly a criminal court and a criminal offense. It's an impeachment court. So if it pleases the court or if The prosecution is sure to ask for the subpoena. May I propose, Sir Presiding Officer, that both sides give us a memoranda in advance so that we can also do our part and study rather than...

